cometkim's benchmark expressions in his own regime (cel-jit PR #233)
one expression, one FIXED activation, ONE evaluation timed; best of 30 batches of >= 20 CPU-ms.
Every ns figure below is USER CPU on the measuring thread, NOT wall clock:
time spent descheduled by other work on the box is not charged to it.

Which evaluator each column runs is printed below, not described here:
re-stating it in prose is what produced four mislabels in this file.

EVALUATOR COLUMNS -- what each one actually runs:
  stock ns   `Value::resolve_value` -- the tree walker, called DIRECTLY
             ! the NON-DEFAULT build. A caller who names no features does not reach this.
  exec ns    `Program::execute` -- the door a caller who names nothing goes through
             ! cel::vm::cel_eval_loop, the bytecode VM
  clean ns   `BoundBatch::collect_on(Tier::Clean)` -- the batch machine's UNTRACED interpreter
             ! NOT `cel::vm`. A plain `match` interpreter over LOWERED COLUMNAR code: registers and banks over flattened `ColumnRef` buffers, no `Value`, no `Arc`, no stack. The VM on this board is `exec`, and it is the only column about `interp.rs`.
  majit ns   `BoundBatch::collect_on(Tier::Jit)` -- the compiled trace
             ! printed only where the settled window entered compiled code on EVERY call; otherwise the cell reads `not entered` and no ratio is derived from it.
  auto ns    `BoundBatch::collect_on(Tier::Auto)` -- the tier the machine picks itself
  raw ns     the batch machine with the bind step already paid

